0..70 Comment "// A derived path operation reads its operand\'s path type off what the"
71..146 Comment "// operand is when its form does not spell one: a parameter by the type its"
147..221 Comment "// binder writes, a call by the result its declaration writes, a recursive"
222..299 Comment "// call by its own function\'s result, and `cong` over a parameter function by"
300..375 Comment "// that function\'s written result, which may read the parameters before it."
376..451 Comment "// In a body and in a type alike, none of these needs a stated type (#423)."
452..529 Comment "// The operations are the HoTT book\'s inverse and composite (Lemmas 2.1.1 and"
530..563 Comment "// 2.1.2) and `ap` (Lemma 2.2.1)."
565..601 Comment "// The circle and the free naturals."
